WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.145
Endpoint Detection and Response helps organizations monitor endpoints,

00:00:04.145 --> 00:00:07.990
detect suspicious behavior, investigate activity, and respond to threats.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:13.050
EDR goes beyond traditional antivirus by focusing on behavior, telemetry, investigation,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:13.750
and response.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.060
It can show process activity, command lines, file changes, network connections, logins,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.820
scripts, and other endpoint events.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.100
EDR supports containment and remediation, but it still requires good deployment, tuning,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.970
monitoring, and human judgment.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.350
EDR is not a magic shield.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.980
It is a visibility and response layer within a broader security program.
